hat implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-middle-allright-defect"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-middle-allright-defect"],"id":"long.thm-middle-allright-defect","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.8 (The tail inequality at a final middle transition)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.8, p. 47, label thm:middle-allright-defect","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose row $D\\ge13$ is middle and all rows after it are right. Let $F_D=D_D\\cup\\{D\\}$ and put\n$$\nC_D=4\\,\\mathrm{rem}(D)-p_D^--4,\\qquad\n \\Theta_D=\\sum_{j\\ge1}c_{F_D}(2D+2+j)2^{-j}.\n$$\nThen $C_D<\\Theta_D$. Since $0\\le\\Theta_D\\le|F_D|$, an estimate in the opposite direction would exclude this scenario. No such reverse estimate is assumed or proved here. Remark 10.8 states the corresponding sufficient hypothesis with the value $-3$ excepted.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-middle-allright-defect","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-middle-allright-defect","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-middle-allright-defect%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.binaryCoeffTail_nonneg%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-middle-allright-defect%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.binaryCoeffTail_nonneg%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.binaryCoeffTail_nonneg"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-middle-allright-defect","id":"